          "block_id": "tile_sql_adv_execution_order_subquery_where.r02.b1",
          "role": "example",
          "text": "Hard-coded: WHERE delivery_time_minutes > 35 — works, but 35 is a guess. Scalar subquery: WHERE delivery_time_minutes > (SELECT AVG(delivery_time_minutes) FROM orders) — the inner query computes the actual average from the data and returns one number; the outer WHERE compares each row against that number. The subquery must return exactly one value to be used in a comparison like > or =.",
